NT07080.definition:
The analysis of the electron density distribution in a molecular system based on the orthonormal natural atomic orbitals. Natural populations, \(n_{i}\left(\rm{A}\right)\) are the occupancies of the natural atomic orbitals. These rigorously satisfy the Pauli exclusion principle: \(0 < n_{i}\left(\rm{A}\right) < 2\). The population of an atom \(n\left(\rm{A}\right)\) is the sum of natural populations \(n\left(\rm{A}\right)=\sum _{\begin{array}{c}
\rm{A}
\end{array}}n_{i}\left(\rm{A}\right)\). A distinguished feature of the NPA method is that it largely resolves the basis set dependence problem encountered in the Mulliken population analysis method.

