15013.definition:
Biological classification of water quality according to five categories:
oligosaprobic: clear, with no or only slight pollution and high dissolved oxygen (DO) content;
p-mesosaprobic: moderately polluted with still high DO content;
x-mesosaprobic: polluted with not very high DO content;
polysaprobic: strongly polluted, with negligible DO content; and
antisaprobic: so polluted that no living organism is capable of living in the water.

